ing"],"y":2017,"c":"pub","j":"Psychological Science","v":"28","i":"8","p":"1041-1055","r":133,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1177/0956797617702501","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1177/0956797617702501"},{"t":"Beyond Beta-Delta: The Emerging Economics of Personal Plans","a":["John Beshears","Katherine L. Milkman","Joshua Schwartzstein"],"y":2016,"c":"pub","j":"American Economic Review","v":"106","i":"5","p":"430-434","r":0,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1257/aer.p20161100","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1257/aer.p20161100"},{"t":"The Effect of Providing Peer Information on Retirement Savings Decisions","a":["JOHN BESHEARS","JAMES J. CHOI","DAVID LAIBSON","BRIGITTE C. MADRIAN","KATHERINE L. MILKMAN"],"y":2015,"c":"pub","j":"Journal of Finance","v":"70","i":"3","p":"1161-1201","r":98,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jofi.12258","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1111/jofi.12258"},{"t":"Liquidity in Retirement Savings Systems: An International Comparison","a":["John Beshears","James J. Choi","Joshua Hurwitz","David Laibson","Brigitte C. Madrian"],"y":2015,"c":"pub","j":"American Economic Review","v":"105","i":"5","p":"420-425","r":0,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1257/aer.p20151004","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1257/aer.p20151004"},{"t":"What makes annuitization more appealing?","a":["John Beshears","James J. Choi","David Laibson","Brigitte C. Madrian","Stephen P. Zeldes"],"y":2014,"c":"pub","j":"Journal of Public Economics","v":"116","p":"2-16","r":23,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpubeco.2013.05.007","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1016/j.jpubeco.2013.05.007"},{"t":"Simplification and saving","a":["John Beshears","James J. Choi","David Laibson","Brigitte C. Madrian"],"y":2013,"c":"pub","j":"Journal of Economic Behavior and Organization","v":"95","p":"130-145","r":52,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jebo.2012.03.007","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1016/j.jebo.2012.03.007"},{"t":"The performance of corporate alliances: Evidence from oil and gas drilling in the Gulf of Mexico","a":["John Beshears"],"y":2013,"c":"pub","j":"Journal of Financial Economics","v":